        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Most homeowners spend roughly $150 to $500 on a pressure washer, and a mid-range electric machine is the right buy for the majority of houses. Gas costs more to buy and keep but is worth it for large concrete areas and heavy grime. Running costs are small either way; the bigger hidden costs are the accessories you will want and the repairs you can avoid with proper winter storage.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If you only need to clean something once, rent. If a job is high, delicate or risky, hire a pro with insurance and a written quote. And if you find yourself paying for either more than once or twice a year, owning a machine is almost certainly the cheaper path. Prices change, so use these ranges as a starting point and check current local prices before you buy or book.
          </p>
